      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Friction stir processing operates below the melting temperature of the constituent materials.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Friction stir processing induces severe localized plastic deformation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Friction stir processing causes dynamic recrystallization.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Friction stir processing produces an ultrafine-grained, refined near-surface layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The processed near-surface layer has a homogenized microstructure and smoother grain boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamic recrystallization and grain refinement improve the distribution of residual stresses.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Microstructural refinement and improved residual-stress distribution reduce hot-cracking propensity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Friction stir processing forms a graded, high-integrity surface composite.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction-stir-processed surface will have greater hardness than fusion-welded and untreated surfaces.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction-stir-processed surface will have better wear resistance than fusion-welded and untreated surfaces.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction-stir-processed surface will have better corrosion resistance than fusion-welded and untreated surfaces.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction-stir-processed surface will exhibit a lower hot-crack density than fusion-welded and untreated surfaces.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The damaged component initially has coarse grains and microstructural inhomogeneities that predispose it to hot cracking during fusion-welding repair.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Traditional fusion-welding repairs retain a coarse, inhomogeneous microstructure prone to hot cracking.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated surfaces have suboptimal hardness and resistance to wear and corrosion.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10730726::web::004::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Localized surface processing can improve the surface without compromising the bulk properties of the component.",
